btd TODO
========

Security
--------

- BR/EDR key size: read the encryption key size (HCI 0x1408) after
  Encryption Change and disconnect below 16; ssp_encryption_changed
  accepts any size.  LE allows 7, consider 16 for HID.
- BR/EDR downgrade: engine_encryption accepts E0 (mode 0x01) for a
  Secure Connections link key (type 7/8); require AES-CCM.
- LE: engine_adv_report matches the configured address by bytes and
  ignores the address type.
- avdtp.c: a peer OPEN while streaming moves to A2DP_S_PEER, after which
  a2dp_stop does nothing; rtp.chan keeps a freed channel and rtp_frame
  uses it.  Key a2dp_stop on rtp.chan, reject OPEN unless configured.
- avdtp_accept/avctp_accept accept several channels before sig/media/
  chan is set; a2dp_down/avrcp_down only clear the tracked one, the
  others keep arg pointing at freed memory.
- Reload during an SDP query: device_reconf frees the device, sdpc_close
  then calls a2dp_sdp with the stale q->dev.
- L2CAP before authentication: no per-connection channel limit, a
  channel that never gets CONFIG_REQ never times out, next_cid wraps
  onto CIDs in use, aclq grows without bound.  l2cap_disconn_req does
  not check the source CID against ch->rcid.
- HOGP discovery (hogp_chars, hogp_descs, hogp_bat_chars) restarts from
  last + 1 without requiring last >= start: a peer can loop it.
- Logging: the HCI trace at -vvv logs LTKs, link keys, SMP keys and HID
  reports (keystrokes).  Redact key-bearing packets, stop dumping ACL
  payloads, clamp the verbosity the control socket accepts.
- bus: root, no pledge, forwards any HCI opcode and any wscons event
  type.  Allow only key events to wskbd, mouse events to wsmouse, and a
  list of HCI opcodes; consider holding the device fds and dropping to
  _btd, RLIMIT_NPROC 0 after the reader fork.  Document the trust
  boundary in btd.8.
- SMP: compare only X when rejecting a reflected public key; reject the
  SC debug public key and the BR debug link key (type 3); validate the
  IO capability and reserved bits of the pairing response.
- Key material: freezero the HCI command structs carrying an LTK or link
  key (hci.c), explicit_bzero the bus buffer, cmac() mb/ob and main's
  stack bond copy, BN_clear_free the DH secret, wipe bond_read's line
  buffer.
- Bonds file: check owner and mode on read, fsync the directory after
  the rename, stricter parsing (%2x accepts 0x, strtoull a minus sign),
  a bad local line half-overwrites the local identity, duplicates kept.
- Privsep: main should validate bond type/keysize and cap the count;
  struct bond and hid_conf cross imsg with TAILQ pointers (heap
  addresses); a duplicate IMSG_DEVFD_* leaks the old fd; drop sendfd in
  main and recvfd in frontend after startup; check daemon()'s return;
  O_CLOEXEC on the lock fd.
- Control socket: getpeereid, root only for reload, log and unpair;
  reject a payload on SHOW; clients set their own pid, used to route
  replies.
- sndio: a missing or badly permissioned cookie makes libsndio mkdir()
  and the frontend pledge abort; check it first, or open sndio only
  with a headset configured.
- sbc_init allows bitpool up to 256; at 251 and above the frame exceeds
  audio.c frame[512].  Cap at 250 and check the length.
- Hostile controller: ACL bytes beyond the 4100 byte buffer are dropped
  silently and desync the stream; no check for a duplicate connection
  handle; acl_num 0 makes aclq grow forever.

Bugs
----

- sdp_send writes the fragment length as the continuation state, the
  caller uses it as an offset: server responses of 3 or more fragments
  repeat or skip data.  Pass cont in and write cont + n.
- rate and bitpool from btd.conf are ignored when the headset sends
  SET_CONFIGURATION (a2dp_parse_config).  Fix or document.
- "headset X { }" is a syntax error: headsetopts_l needs an option.
- btd.c: a SIGHUP reload logs at debug, a btctl reload at info.

Daemon conventions
------------------

- Makefile: regress in SUBDIR runs the tests on a plain make; add it
  only for regress, clean, cleandir and obj.
- daemon(1, 0): with a relative -f the unveil and reload use /.
- log_init runs before the device opens: startup errors go to syslog
  only.  Move it right before daemon().
- main_reload ignores send errors; return them and keep the old config.
- btd.c: missing break after main_shutdown in the signal handler;
  main_sendall declared, not defined; imsgbuf_flush results ignored in
  main_imsg_send_ipc_sockets; verbosity set before parse_config.
- parse.y: log_getverbose() == 1 / == 2 should be >=; check_file_secrecy
  is dead code; /*empty*/ -> /* empty */.
- frontend: imsgbuf_write before imsgbuf_clear at shutdown.
- btctl: no "log debug" level, -vvv unreachable at runtime.
- style(9): 28 lines over 80 columns; module-local functions not
  static; I2S macro return without parentheses; control.c include
  order.
- log.c, log.h: drop the copied $OpenBSD$ IDs and the unused SMALL
  block.
- regress: NOMAN is redundant; add a parse regress with -nv golden
  files; crypto: f4 with z 0x80/0x81, a known P-256 key pair, X-only
  reflection, debug key.

Documentation
-------------

- btd.8:
  - only 2357:0604 is known, other RTL8761BU need "firmware".
  - document SIGHUP, and that device and firmware need a restart.
  - keyboard LEDs and /dev/wskbd0, /dev/btd.lock in FILES.
  - the engine pledges "stdio recvfd", not "stdio".
  - the sndiod sub-device must be named mon; "the SBC rate" is the
    configured rate.
  - PAIRING and AUDIO as .Ss, HOTPLUG under EXAMPLES; add STANDARDS
    (Core, HOGP, BAS, A2DP, AVDTP, AVRCP, RFC 3550), AUTHORS.
  - SEE ALSO sndioctl 1, hotplugd 8; only usb0 to usb9 are scanned;
    LE legacy pairing is refused; the local name is the hostname.
- btd.conf.5: firmware is Realtek only; add a macro example and a lead-in
  before the keywords; colon-separated, two digits per octet; .Cm for
  the rates; describe the FILES entry; mention the audio role.
- btctl.8: "log verbose" is level 2 (-vv).
- Comments: hci_cmd_noreply should say msec holds the queue; capitalise
  avdtp.c and engine.c one-liners; rtp_frame comment misses the
  RTP_MAX_FRAMES flush and MTU drop; btd.h "/* engine */" covers shared
  constants; bond.c format comment omits blank and # lines; bus.c
  "X" -> "the X server"; hid_test "hand made" -> "hand-made".
- README: give the dropped-audio paragraph its own heading;
  "privilege-separated"; the SBC regress is skipped without ffmpeg.
- Changes: 0.1 is unreleased but lists fixes to earlier behaviour.
